Package: planscanR
Title: Retrieve Environmental-Assessment Records From European Portals
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Bart", "Hoekstra", email = "mail@barthoekstra.nl", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A unified R interface for fetching environmental-assessment
    records (EIA, SEA, follow-up advice) from European national portals into
    one consistent table, with an on-disk cache for offline re-use. Handlers
    ship for the Netherlands (Commissie m.e.r.), Germany (UVP-Verbund),
    France (Projets-Environnement),
    Austria (Umweltbundesamt UVP-DB), Denmark (EA-Hub), Belgium (Flanders;
    MER-register), Estonia (Keskkonnaamet KOTKAS; KMH + KSH), Finland
    (ymparisto.fi; EIA/YVA only), Bulgaria
    (МОСВ registers; ОВОС + ЕО), the Czech Republic (CENIA EIA/SEA;
    domestic registers only), Croatia (Ministry of Environment CMS
    pages; PUO + SPUO), Greece (ΗΠΜ / EPRM; AEPO permit decisions
    only), Iceland (Skipulagsgátt GraphQL; cases from ~June 2023
    onward), Ireland (gov.ie EIA Portal; ArcGIS REST; EIA only,
    notice PDFs with the full EIAR off-portal), Slovenia (gov.si
    registers; bulk JSON exports; EIA screening + SEA/CPVO),
    Portugal (APA SIAIA; HTML register; AIA / project-level EIA only,
    SEA/AAE in a separate register), the United Kingdom (Planning
    Inspectorate National Infrastructure Consenting; bulk CSV export;
    NSIP only, each with a statutory Environmental Statement),
    Italy (MASE va.mite.gov.it; HTML register; VIA project EIA + VAS
    plan SEA), Slovakia (enviroportal.sk; API Platform JSON;
    EIA + SEA in one register, tagged by the zbierka law string), and
    Norway (NVE nve.no; JSON list + HTML detail; energy/water
    concession cases carrying the konsekvensutredning EIA documents).
    Optional
    fetch-time scoring of records by topic relevance is delegated to the
    companion 'planscanR.screen' package. Developed for the BIOGAIN project
    to support Net Biodiversity Gain in spatial energy planning.
